OL,3,GNEWSAAsian hornet hunt leads to nest
OL,4,Adiscovery
OL,5,
OL,6,FBeekeepers who feared a damaging new
OL,7,Farrival of Asian hornets in the Greater
OL,8,FManchester area helped track down their
OL,9,Fnest after sightings sparked an urgent
OL,10,Fsearch.
OL,12,FThe nest of the non-native invasive
OL,13,Finsects, which prey on honey bees and
OL,14,Fthreatens biodiversity, was found in
OL,15,FOldham, after local keepers worked with
OL,16,Fgovernment bee inspectors to trace them
OL,17,Fusing GPS trackers and food traps.
OL,19,FThe Asian hornets were first spotted
OL,20,Fthree weeks ago in Oldham, prompting
OL,21,Fconcerns the species may be spreading
OL,22,Ffurther north.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,410,400,260,160,0,100
